var s=Object.defineProperty;var n=(o,e)=>{for(var t in e)s(o,t,{get:e[t],enumerable:!0})};var r=[{text:"**Let's get your home in**, the first thing a new home shows, has the demo house turning behind it in the evening with its lights on, and its ways to start as buttons with a picture each (**Start from a house type** says it is the quickest). It holds still on Tablet graphics and with reduced motion.",anchor:"install"},{text:"**A floor plan picture that shows every storey** (as most estate agents' plans do): **Find the rooms** tells the drawings apart, asks **Which one is this floor?**, and leaves out the paper between them. After **Add these rooms**, **Add it as the floor above** puts the next drawing on a new storey, its rooms and the picture moved to stand over the floor below.",anchor:"trace-a-floor-plan-picture"},{text:"The online demo opens by itself: the house turns slowly and its roofs come off to show the rooms and who is in them, with a line on what to try (in its 14 languages), until it is touched. Its tour opens on the open house, its rooms lighting up one by one, and a chapter's title dims the house behind it so it can be read over a floor full of labels.",anchor:null},{text:"After setting VirtuHome up, Home Assistant's dialog says where it is (the sidebar), and the setup text names the ways to get a home in.",anchor:null},{text:"**House types come furnished and show in 3D while you choose.** Picking a house type shows it in the 3D view at once, its roofs off, and follows the width, depth and side as you set them; nothing changes until **Use this house type**. **With furniture** (on to start with) puts a sofa and TV, a table and chairs, kitchen units with a sink and cooker, beds, wardrobes and a bath or shower in their rooms, against walls that are free for them at the home's size.",anchor:"start-from-a-house-type"},{text:"**The editor's Home tab folds into parts** under their headings (Getting started, Check my setup, Demo home, house type, import, Devices, Outside walls, Roof, Sun and weather, Floors, Energy, People, Top bar, Plan file, Help), instead of one long page. What the last step did is listed at the top.",anchor:null},{text:"**A home just set up opens with its roofs off**, once, on the device it was set up on, so its rooms and devices are the first thing seen. The Roof button puts them back.",anchor:null},{text:"**On a phone the buttons on the right keep behind one** (**More buttons**), leaving the screen to the house; Search stays out.",anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"A selected room starts with its **Name** and **Area**, in 3D and in the 2D plan, so rooms traced from a picture are named where they are tapped. A room still called Room 3 or New room takes the area's name when it is linked.",anchor:"draw-it-in-the-2d-plan"}];export{n as a,r as b};
